{"title":"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The first four terms in an arithmetic sequence are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3da9f8c7fe0473fdd6f8597eff61d71fedda430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/643e1765342cf3807fd7d130ee679b71ecd4789b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e32f96b310bbe6cd6981b6c1da83fe7905ea3116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"12\" height=\"36\" />, in that order. What is the fifth term? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/1/c014255fe627d7cc95083f6bb6a360f3f95519b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ -\\frac{15}{8}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ -\\frac{6}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 0\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{27}{20}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{123}{40}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"444\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The difference between consecutive terms is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/2/962064d8b7ad50de4d4ed4a7e416d4735aa33af3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-y)-(x+y)=-2y.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"18\" /> Therefore we can also express the third and fourth terms as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/d/90dc5734a1f1634f502f1edef4c58a32a729f5a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/7/7d7fa576a222beed25273e0d50392e2f1ddfc396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-5y.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> Then we can set them equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e32f96b310bbe6cd6981b6c1da83fe7905ea3116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"12\" height=\"36\" /> because they are the same thing.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c82bd1e7f2934c3e57e62eb6a3358bf2540281c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} xy&amp;=x-3y\\\\ xy-x&amp;=-3y\\\\ x(y-1)&amp;=-3y\\\\ x&amp;=\\frac{-3y}{y-1} \\end{align*}\" width=\"139\" height=\"115\" />\n</p><p>Substitute into our other equation.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/7447ff4042273b628b683c0be7a6adb782094cc4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x}{y}=x-5y\\]\" width=\"87\" height=\"36\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/f/eafd224e1b0406671c0ea78a89f70250ab4d9598.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{-3}{y-1}=\\frac{-3y}{y-1}-5y\\]\" width=\"152\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/2/582e642d7ac3fe394341c104bb678404cf1937d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-3=-3y-5y(y-1)\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/c/4fc65b027cacf27699496e8f7a46167eb301ea72.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0=5y^2-2y-3\\]\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/2715b828ebf0e900ba0d1a4a4409393b2d5c9683.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0=(5y+3)(y-1)\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/f/2bf85034e5c754150e8e99435ec811627279e560.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=-\\frac35, 1\\]\" width=\"76\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because then the first term would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/cccb103143393c0119f5ab61d6d53a852ce70fcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> and the second term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4baf6d4b1cfa69b68b3204b5e2eba0c5755fe20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> while the last two terms would be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc3be04db73828946870d3ccc6d122395a4bacf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e77c6b44e7fd1f17c8fca2b615714cfe05fe26c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-\\frac35.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"64\" height=\"37\" /> Substituting the value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> into any of the equations, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/9/2a9522918d9a7fea8f82c1f05a6e83e590261f9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-\\frac98.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"65\" height=\"37\" /> Finally,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/e/55e30872e72c0aa052d66c068d2af833a675a508.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x}{y}-2y=\\frac{9\\cdot 5}{8\\cdot 3}+\\frac{6}{5}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{123}{40}}\\]\" width=\"248\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because this is an arithmetic sequence, we conclude from the first two terms that the common difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/e/c6efdf74a0d002b82228e7dd182b0b39d2985cf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/a/35a522134032a54e9bb0c4c01eab81fe500ec100.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy = x-3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/d/dadc64f272335ec822777c99ec2a8e424b450da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}=x-5y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"89\" height=\"36\" />. If we multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e32f96b310bbe6cd6981b6c1da83fe7905ea3116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"12\" height=\"36\" />, we see: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/7/f97f219818d31474ba3653c55f1322cb50956c7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy\\cdot\\frac{x}{y} = (x-3y)(x-5y) = x^2 - 8xy + 15y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"355\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/645b6d363cfdb5bc42798504fce81dc25c05fc08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy\\cdot\\frac{x}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"49\" height=\"38\" />, by basic multiplication, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, we have \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/8/9e8d0d1990f89f1dfa521424151d17de24eff867.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 = x^2 - 8xy + 15y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"170\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/3/e63a350c9d52b107928b2b21d346f9b92d659a97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8xy = 15y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/c/6ec72ef74f5175074cb2f4b4583b61a872b29d9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8x = 15y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/48521e590d51efcbedfacc39e471c34866b393dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{15y}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Now that we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, we substitute in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/7/68783f8ea6614c5e6d7012edc72d898e6c9b52b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15y}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"34\" height=\"38\" /> in for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e32f96b310bbe6cd6981b6c1da83fe7905ea3116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"12\" height=\"36\" /> (the fourth term). This leaves us with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/b/84b014dab307414317aa503091817facf665085a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{15y}{8}}{y} = \\frac{15}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"77\" height=\"46\" />. \n</p><p>Recall that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e32f96b310bbe6cd6981b6c1da83fe7905ea3116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"12\" height=\"36\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/5/8b5e064a59bf8781bd05292cfd91942ec7f9f03f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 5y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d8813daef179dc5b9fe5e08b730f659d7fc8c7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 5y = \\frac{15}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"100\" height=\"38\" />. Substitute in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c6c840d3b2f21ec688bca3ba8850a8c77990b48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> in for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and we see:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/6/746c736a35d512fe97f5003f0701d8cb81d1c5a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15y}{8} - 5y = \\frac{15}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"121\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/9/e490cc81cde00aa79992c32ac94994eb42d0b518.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15y - 40y = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/b/11b3556561ad475a3824e1fff34628837185b2ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{15}{-25} = \\frac{-3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"123\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Aha! This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/c/26cab3f0704de3232f601b03d02a45d46103c172.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />, the common difference, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/5/b959727b797e8351e8a6b44525904a8d818e04b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot y = 2\\cdot \\frac{-3}{5} = \\frac{-6}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"159\" height=\"38\" />. Now, all we need to do is find the fifth term, which is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/6/e968cee1b694963fd2aa6a2680a5ca1ebd04120d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}-2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"54\" height=\"36\" />. We can substitute known values to solve: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/7/1f70f157b3e7dca95dc687fe3375bda2a21d4a39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}-2y = \\frac{15}{8} - \\frac{-6}{5} = \\frac{15}{8} + \\frac{6}{5} = \\frac{75 + 48}{40} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{123}{40}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"421\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~SXWang\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the first two terms, we can figure out the common difference, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/9/059905ffb02a61cae09496134a1ca0d1ca6b6af7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-y-(x+y)=-2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"180\" height=\"20\" />.\nThis means that the third, fourth and fifth terms are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/d/90dc5734a1f1634f502f1edef4c58a32a729f5a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5ecd7bcf42b57ed637b7c878d904872585c8a36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-5y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f510d7ee2b968b5f6ca5f90931a0b11cb7e8e972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-7y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>The third term is also equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" />, so \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/c/0acae0a3cd5d4440bbfa1b9efb11ae82b08d23b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy=x-3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" />, which can be rearranged to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8b6346a3314b8a5aa393ed70422ef4e2cf9b4cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy+3y=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Dividing by y, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/d/56d3b2aa633954af13f8914f05259d7f70c977e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+3=\\frac{x}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e32f96b310bbe6cd6981b6c1da83fe7905ea3116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"12\" height=\"36\" /> happens to be the fourth term. Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/0/910d8c9e810e0c1a8223e3bc900ed7f97b281264.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}=x-5y=x+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"158\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/5/0d5173563db4a2d1020fbb48d0c978810a120e99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-5y=x+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/7/367e0bea15b767f27e40c2ec366b8319618f4ee0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-5y=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/9/4292ea7351b6fe1fb721a2c7ef90d9048eed52c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-\\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Now that we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, we can substitute it into an equation above, like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/6/4d669d98678b67f76bb8e0f79aba4c96bfb8be74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}=x+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f96324b6fd17aabcbc730f577d9ac5b5a4eb1317.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{\\frac{-3}{5}}=x+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"93\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/8/2682c67026c692bedfe80f914f9b6c9b9eebcda8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{5x}{3}=x+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/d/0ed9567b193aca527dee9c9861af63f409aca657.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{5x+3x}{3}=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/f/14ffe35e4fef7358e6fea6e97ce204030ff59d8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{8x}{3}=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/8/6289cf5e2bd2d6315d80d7ababef3f31505f30a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8x=-9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"69\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/d/2ed843d9a452c11f8a58455fb47327dc0b3ba7fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{-9}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>As mentioned earlier, the fifth term we want in the end is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f510d7ee2b968b5f6ca5f90931a0b11cb7e8e972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-7y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />. Substitute some more and...\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c1787edb6d7d5b7ec713ebdf3bf0984c2e0a0184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-9}{8}-7(\\frac{-3}{5})=\\frac{-9\\cdot5}{8\\cdot5}+\\frac{-3\\cdot-7\\cdot8}{5\\cdot8}=\\frac{-45}{40}+\\frac{168}{40}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{123}{40}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"497\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>(Alternatively, like the above solutions suggest, you could also use the admittedly easier <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/6/e968cee1b694963fd2aa6a2680a5ca1ebd04120d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}-2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"54\" height=\"36\" /> as the final step.)\n</p><p>~ a seesaw named owlly81 ~\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wzNnrj51BAQ\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wzNnrj51BAQ</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B\">2003 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2